{"timestamp": "2025-07-30T14:04:54.833922", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "    _DOWN = 0\n    _UP = 1\n    _LEFT = 2\n    _RIGHT = 3\n    _USE = 4\n\n    actions = []\n    current_state = env._current_state  # Get the initial state for planning\n\n    cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n    index_map = cookbook.index\n\n    # Define a recursive helper function to generate actions for a single item.\n    # This helper does not simulate inventory changes or agent position changes during planning.\n    # It assumes the initial `current_state` for all grid and inventory lookups,\n    # leading to a potentially suboptimal but functional action sequence.\n    def _get_actions_for_item(target_item_id):\n        item_actions = []\n\n        # 1. Check if the item is already in the initial inventory.\n        # This prevents infinite recursion if an item can be crafted from itself (shouldn't happen with valid recipes)\n        # or if the goal item is already present.\n        if current_state.inventory[target_item_id] > 0:\n            return []  # Already have it, no actions needed for this instance\n\n        # 2. Check if the item is a primitive resource that can be picked up.\n        if target_item_id in cookbook.primitives:\n            # Need to find and \"use\" (pick up) the primitive from the grid.\n            grid = current_state.grid\n            current_pos_for_planning = current_state.pos\n\n            target_x, target_y = -1, -1\n            # Simple search for the item on the entire grid.\n            # Assumes the item is reachable and only one instance is needed/considered.\n            for y in range(grid.shape[1]):  # Iterate rows (height)\n                for x in range(grid.shape[0]):  # Iterate columns (width)\n                    if grid[x, y, target_item_id] > 0:\n                        target_x, target_y = x, y\n                        break\n                if target_x != -1:\n                    break\n\n            if target_x != -1:\n                # Generate moves to target_x, target_y from current_pos_for_planning.\n                # This uses a simple Manhattan distance movement, ignoring obstacles.\n                dx = target_x - current_pos_for_planning[0]\n                dy = target_y - current_pos_for_planning[1]\n\n                for _ in range(abs(dx)):\n                    item_actions.append(_RIGHT if dx > 0 else _LEFT)\n                for _ in range(abs(dy)):\n                    item_actions.append(_UP if dy > 0 else _DOWN)\n\n                item_actions.append(_USE)  # Use action to pick up the primitive.\n                return item_actions\n            else:\n                return []  # Primitive not found on the grid.\n\n        # 3. Check if the item can be crafted (is a recipe output).\n        if target_item_id in cookbook.recipes:\n            recipe = cookbook.recipes[target_item_id]\n\n            workshop_id = None\n            ingredients_needed = {}\n\n            # Parse recipe ingredients and any required workshop.\n            for ing_id_or_key, count in recipe.items():\n                if ing_id_or_key == \"_key\":\n                    # This is the workshop required for crafting (e.g., 'workbench')\n                    workshop_name = count\n                    workshop_id = index_map[workshop_name]\n                else:\n                    ingredients_needed[ing_id_or_key] = count\n\n            # Recursively gather actions for all ingredients.\n            for ing_id, required_count in ingredients_needed.items():\n                # Important: This simplified planner does not track inventory changes during planning.\n                # Thus, if a recipe needs `N` units of an ingredient, it will generate `N` sets of actions\n                # to obtain that ingredient, even if one set would suffice to satisfy all needs.\n                # This can lead to redundant actions but ensures all requirements are \"planned\" for.\n                for _ in range(required_count):\n                    ing_actions = _get_actions_for_item(ing_id)\n                    if not ing_actions:\n                        # Cannot craft/get this ingredient, so the main item cannot be crafted.\n                        return []\n                    item_actions.extend(ing_actions)\n\n            # After gathering all ingredients, add actions for using the workshop if required.\n            if workshop_id is not None:\n                grid = current_state.grid\n                current_pos_for_planning = current_state.pos\n\n                target_x, target_y = -1, -1\n                # Search for the workshop on the grid.\n                for y in range(grid.shape[1]):\n                    for x in range(grid.shape[0]):\n                        if grid[x, y, workshop_id] > 0:\n                            target_x, target_y = x, y\n                            break\n                    if target_x != -1:\n                        break\n\n                if target_x != -1:\n                    # Move to the workshop location.\n                    dx = target_x - current_pos_for_planning[0]\n                    dy = target_y - current_pos_for_planning[1]\n\n                    for _ in range(abs(dx)):\n                        item_actions.append(_RIGHT if dx > 0 else _LEFT)\n                    for _ in range(abs(dy)):\n                        item_actions.append(_UP if dy > 0 else _DOWN)\n\n                    item_actions.append(_USE)  # Use the workshop to perform the craft.\n                else:\n                    return []  # Workshop not found on the grid.\n\n            return item_actions\n\n        # 4. Check if the item is an environment object that can be \"used\" directly (e.g., water, stone).\n        # These are typically in `non_grabbable_indices` and require interaction.\n        if target_item_id in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n            # Find the item on the grid, move to it, and use it.\n            grid = current_state.grid\n            current_pos_for_planning = current_state.pos\n\n            target_x, target_y = -1, -1\n            for y in range(grid.shape[1]):\n                for x in range(grid.shape[0]):\n                    if grid[x, y, target_item_id] > 0:\n                        target_x, target_y = x, y\n                        break\n                if target_x != -1:\n                    break\n\n            if target_x != -1:\n                dx = target_x - current_pos_for_planning[0]\n                dy = target_y - current_pos_for_planning[1]\n\n                for _ in range(abs(dx)):\n                    item_actions.append(_RIGHT if dx > 0 else _LEFT)\n                for _ in range(abs(dy)):\n                    item_actions.append(_UP if dy > 0 else _DOWN)\n                item_actions.append(_USE)\n                return item_actions\n            else:\n                return []  # Item not found in the environment.\n\n        # If the item is neither a primitive, a craftable recipe output, nor a usable environment object,\n        # then it's considered uncraftable/unobtainable by this function's logic.\n        return []\n\n    # Initial call to the recursive helper function for the main goal item.\n    actions = _get_actions_for_item(item)\n    return actions", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": -1}}
